      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": null,
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "<div style=\"padding:10px 16px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.65;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n  <strong>Network O11y \u2014 Device Details</strong> is a per-device drill-down for a single\n  SR Linux switch. Select a node with the <em>Device</em> variable above. Panels cover\n  CPU and memory utilisation, per-interface traffic rates and errors, BGP neighbour state,\n  and a live syslog event feed from the device.\n</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">\n  <strong>Telemetry pipeline:</strong>\n  CPU, memory, and BGP metrics come from <strong>gNMI streaming telemetry</strong> \u2014 gnmic\n  subscribes to each SR Linux gNMI endpoint, exports the data as Prometheus metrics, and\n  Alloy scrapes them every 30 s. Interface traffic counters are collected separately by\n  Alloy via <strong>SNMP v2c</strong> polling (60 s interval). Syslog events are forwarded\n  by the SR Linux rsyslog daemon over <strong>UDP 6514</strong> directly to Alloy's Loki\n  receiver (ClusterIP), then shipped to Grafana Cloud Loki.\n</p>\n</div>",
        "mode": "html"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "10.0.0",
      "transparent": true
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
